n the perinuclear/cytoplasmic region. Use this image to show subcellular localization of the label and to estimate size/spacing (scale bar = 20 \u03bcm).\n[Figure] Fluorescence micrograph of an adherent cell monolayer showing blue-stained nuclei and red cytoplasmic/membrane signal with occasional yellow puncta. Scale bar = 20 \u00b5m (lower right). Use to verify staining quality, cell morphology and monolayer coverage before proceeding with image analysis or cell counting.\n[Figure] Screenshot of the \"Find Nuclei\" module: Channel = HOECHST 3325, ROI Population = None, Method = B, Output Population = Nuclei. The right panel shows the detection overlay with each nucleus outlined in colored contours; confirm outlines correctly mark nuclei before continuing.\n[Figure] Screenshot of the image-analysis step \"Select Population\" in the pipeline: left pane shows module order (Input Image \u2192 Find Nuclei \u2192 Select Population \u2192 Find Cytoplasm \u2026) with \"Method: Common Filter\" and \"Remove Border Objects\" checked and Output Population = \"Nuclei Selected.\" Right pane is the fluorescence image with segmentation overlays: green outlines = nuclei selected, red = excluded/border objects.\n[Figure] Screenshot of the analysis pane and result: the Find Cytoplasm module (left) set to Channel = \"CellMask Deep\", Nuclei = \"Nuclei Selected\", Method = \"A\". The right panel shows the grayscale fluorescence image with multicolored outlines marking segmented cytoplasm/cell boundaries. This indicates cytoplasm was computed from the selected nuclei using Method A on the CellMask Deep channel; colored contours show accepted cell ROIs (Population: Nuclei Selected).\n[Figure] Screenshot of the image-analysis workflow and a segmentation overlay: the left panel lists pipeline steps (Input Image \u2192 Find Nuclei \u2192 Select Population \u2192 Find Cytoplasm \u2192 Calculate Intensity Properties \u2192 Find Spots \u2192 Define Results) and parameter choices (Channel: Alexa 594; Population: Nuclei Selected; Region: Cytoplasm; Method: Standard). The right panel shows fluorescent cells with colored outlines marking detected nuclei and cytoplasm, demonstrating successful segmentation used for downstream intensity measurements.\n[Figure] Screenshot of the pipeline's \"Find Spots\" step: left pane shows settings \u2014 Channel: Alexa 594; ROI Population: Nuclei Selected; ROI Region: Cytoplasm; Method: B; Output Population: Spots. Right pane displays detected nuclei and cytoplasm outlines with multicolored spot detections overlaid, confirming spots were called inside cytoplasmic ROIs.\n[Figure] Screenshot of the analysis GUI showing detected nuclei overlaid with colored outlines (right) and the \"Define Results\" panel (left). The panel lists measurements to export for the selected population (\"Nuclei Selected\") \u2014 e.g. Number of Objects (checked), Alexa 594 mean intensity, Total Spot Area (Mean), Relative Spot Intensity, Number of Spots and Spots per Area of Cytoplasm. The image demonstrates object detection and which result fields will be recorded.", "type": "Document"}}